USAGE:
    kern <COMMAND> [ARGS]

COMMANDS:
  Essentials
    box <name> (--rootfs <dir>|--image <ref>) [opts] [-- CMD...]   Run CMD in a sandbox
    box <name> [PROFILE…] --plan                                   Preview the isolation sequence + device grants
    run [opts] <image> [CMD...]                                    Run CMD in a sandbox from <image>, docker run's shape (box's options)
    limit [--memory M] [--cpus N] [vcpu:PROFILE] [--] CMD...       Run CMD on this host under CPU/mem caps (no sandbox)
    limit --landlock-rw <path> [--] CMD...                         Confine CMD's writes to <path> (kernel LSM, no sandbox)
    exec <name> [-i|-t|-it] [-u <user>] [--env K=V] [-w <dir>] [--] [CMD...]  Run CMD in a running box
    ps [-a] [--json] [-q] [--filter name=|status=|id=|label=|pod=|health=] [--format T] [--no-trunc] [--last N|-n N]  List boxes (-a also lists recently-exited: transient, gc-reaped, no name hold)
    logs <name>|--all [--tail N] [-f|--follow] [-t|--timestamps] [--since T] [--until T]  Show a box's output
    stop [-t N] <name>... | --all                                  Stop box(es), or all; -t: seconds before the kill

  Images
    search <query> [--json]                                        Search the public image registry
    pull <image> [-q|--quiet]                                      Fetch an image into the cache (`--image` uses it)
    pull <image> --dest <dir> [--platform os/arch]                 Extract a rootfs instead, for `--rootfs`
    push <local-ref> [as <remote-ref>]                             Publish a cached image to a registry
    tag <src> <dst>                                                Give a cached image a second name
    commit <box> <image>                                           Snapshot a running box's fs into a reusable image (warm start)
    build -t <name> [-t <name>…] [-f <file>] [--build-arg K=V] [--target S] [ctx|-]  Build a local image; without -f it reads a Containerfile, else a Dockerfile (--target: stop at that `FROM … AS S` stage; `-` or -f -: from stdin)
    build --check [-f <file>] [--build-arg K=V] [ctx]              Say what kern does with every instruction of that file, and build NOTHING
    images [<repo>] [--json] [--digests] [--filter K=V] [--format T]  List pulled (cached) images (<repo> = --filter reference=<repo>)
    image ls|inspect|rm|pull|push|tag|save|load|build             The same verbs grouped under `image` (one parser each, not a second)
    image history <image> [--json] [--no-trunc] [-q]              The image's steps, newest first, with each layer's compressed size
    rmi [-f] <image>...                                            Remove cached images (frees unshared layers); -f also one a box uses
    save <image> [-o file]                                         Export an image to a tar (the common image-archive format)
    load [-i file]                                                 Import an image from a tar (the common image-archive format)
    builds [<tag>] [--status S] [-n N] [--json]                    List past builds; S is ok|warn|failed|running|interrupted
    build logs|inspect|rm|prune <id>                               Inspect/manage build-history records

  Manage boxes
    top                                                            Interactive task manager (TUI): host, every GPU, boxes, sandboxes (finished too)
    top --json [--tab T,..] [--stream [--interval S]]               The same frames as JSON for a program: one, or one a line every S s (NDJSON)
    stats [--json] [--no-stream] [name...]                         Per-box memory + CPU (always a snapshot; --no-stream names that, `kern top` is the live view)
    sandbox ls [--json] | history [-n N] [--failed] [--all] [--json] | stats [--all] [--json]  The SDK and MCP sandboxes: running now, finished, outcomes
    sandbox show [<box>] [-n N] [--json]                         The code SDK sandboxes ran and their output (kept with the history)
    sandbox keep|clear [memory|disk|off]                             Where the finished ones are kept (default memory: until reboot), or remove them
    inspect <name> [--json] [-f|--format T]                        Full detail for one box; -f renders a Go-style template
    port <box> [<container-port>[/tcp|/udp]]                       Host address serving that box port, or every mapping it has
    attach <name>                                                  Stream a box's output live (Ctrl-C detaches)
    cp [-L] <box>:<src> <dst> | [-L] <src> <box>:<dst>               Copy files or directories host<->box (- = a tar on stdout/stdin; -L follows a symlink SRC)
    pause <name>... | --all                                        Freeze box(es) (cgroup freezer)
    unpause <name>... | --all                                      Thaw frozen box(es)
    kill [-s SIGNAL] <name>... | killall                           Kill box(es) at once (SIGKILL), or send SIGNAL to the init
    create [OPTIONS] IMAGE [CMD...]                                A kept box recorded and not started (box's options, --name N); prints its name
    start [-a] <name>...                                           Run a `box --keep`/`create` box again, on the layer it left behind; -a follows its output
    restart [-t N] <name>...                                       Stop a kept box and start it again, or start it if stopped (N: seconds before the kill)
    rm [-f] <name>...                                              Remove a stopped or exited box and its record (`--keep`: its layer too); -f stops a running one first
    rename <old> <new>                                             Give a box (running or kept) a new name
    update [--memory M] [--cpus N] [--pids-limit P] [--timeout S] <box>  Change a box's caps: live when running (needs delegated cgroup), and a kept box's record
    wait <box>...                                                  Wait for box(es) to exit and print the code; one that already exited answers at once
    diff <box> [--json]                                            List filesystem changes vs the image (C/D); a kept box's too, running or not
    export <box> [-o file]                                         A running box's filesystem as a tar (stdout without -o)
    container <verb> ...                                           The box verbs under one name (container ls = ps; not top/prune)
    compat docker (-- CMD...|link <dir>|unlink <dir>|status)        Run CMD with `docker` answered by kern (kern-docker), or a recorded `docker` link
    unshare [--] [CMD...]                                          Run CMD (default: your shell) with the ids a box's files carry on disk
    compat docker (enable|disable|serve)                           The Docker API on a socket of this user, answered by kern (Testcontainers)
    proxy (trust|untrust|status)                                   HTTPS for the .localhost names, with kern's own local CA
    events                                                         Stream box start/die/rename events (Ctrl-C; best-effort)
    prune                                                          Remove a stopped box's leftovers: logs, health, environment, and the recorded exit code
    gc [--images]                                                  Cleanup: prune + scratch + build layers. --images DELETES every cached image
    recover                                                        Reclaim orphaned scratch of dead boxes (also done by gc)
    history [-n N]                                                 Recently-run boxes

  Multi-box
    compose [<file>] [up|down|stop|start|restart|ps|logs|build|pull|config|watch|port|systemd|run|cp|exec|wait|events|images|push|rm|top|version|kill]  Run a stack (kern TOML or a compose file); [--profile P] selects optional services
    up [--no-pod|--pod|--bridge] [-d] / down                        Bring up / tear down the stack (--no-pod: a namespace per service, peers through relays; --pod: one shared)
    compose <file> watch [service...]                              Rebuild + restart ONE service when its `build:` context changes
    compose <file> port <service> <container-port>                 Print the host address serving that box port (non-zero if none)
    compose <file> run [--rm] [--no-deps] <service> [cmd...]       One-off box from a service definition, in the foreground; its exit code is kern's
    compose <file> cp <service>:<path> <dst> | <src> <service>:<path>  Copy a file in or out, naming the SERVICE rather than the box
    compose <file> exec [-T] <service> <cmd...>                     Run a command in a RUNNING service; its exit code is kern's
    compose <file> ps [-q] [--services] [--format json|T]          Docker's table (NAME IMAGE COMMAND SERVICE CREATED STATUS PORTS); -q ids, json NDJSON
    compose <file> config [service...] [--format yaml|json] [--services|--images|--volumes|--networks|--profiles|--environment|--variables|--hash S] [--no-interpolate] [-q] [-o F]  The project as Docker Compose prints it; kern's summary on stderr
    up [-d] [--wait [--wait-timeout N]] / down [-v] [--remove-orphans]  --wait holds until every service is ready (-d alone exits 0 if one dies at once); down -v deletes this project's named volumes
    up [--abort-on-container-exit] [--exit-code-from <service>]        Stop the stack when a service exits, and adopt that service's status
    pod create <name> [--no-outbound] [--no-uid-range] [--bridge <cidr>]...  Shared-network pod: peers reach each other by name.
    pod ls [--json] | pod rm <name>                                List pods, or remove one
    network create <name> | network ls [--json] | network inspect <name> [--json] [-f T] | network rm <name>  A network shared between projects (compose `external: true`); alias: net

  Config & storage
    config [list [--json]|edit|setup|probe|clear]                  List resource profiles; manage kern.toml (alias: cfg)
    config add <kind:name> [--flags]                               Create a profile (vcpu/vgpio/vdisk), CLI twin of `kern top`
    config rm <kind:name>                                          Delete a profile
    config set <key> <value>                                       Set a [kern] key, e.g. log_max_size 10m, build_keep 200, log_keep_ended 24h
    config get [<key>] [--json]                                    The [kern] keys and their values; one key prints its value, exit 1 if unset, 3 if kern.toml does not parse
    config unset <key>                                             Remove a [kern] key, back to kern's default
    validate [path]                                                Check a kern.toml
    self-update [--check [--json]] [--to X.Y.Z] [--rollback]       Replace kern with a newer SIGNED release (keeps the old one for --rollback)
    uninstall [--yes] [--keep-images]                              Remove everything kern created (lists it first)
    examples                                                       Print an example kern.toml (alias: example)
    volume <create|rm|edit|prune> / <ls|inspect> [--json]          Manage named volumes (alias: vol)
    login [registry] [--username U] [--password-stdin|--password P] / logout [registry]  Registry credentials (private pulls)

  Diagnostics
    doctor [--apparmor-profile]                                    Preflight: will boxes run here?
    probe                                                          Host resources you can put in kern.toml
    info                                                           Runtime + host snapshot
    version [--json]                                               kern's version; --json adds the `kern top --json` schema
    bench (--image <ref>|--rootfs <dir>) [--bind-rootfs] [-n N] [--compare docker|podman] [--json]  Time box start→exit latency
    completions <bash|zsh|fish>                                    Print a shell-completion script


OPTIONS:
    Per verb, where you are asking about it: kern <verb> --help (box, run, limit, compose, pod, volume, image, config, top)

Docs & issues: https://github.com/getkern/kern
